      {
        "id": "card_f13c95aa01ca99f839af0eff6604eab2e122f4e003b9a308d68b81d3ac2a1912",
        "source": {
          "repository": "xerj-org/xerj",
          "commit": "1557de2f5be981d9db441969201c92a8af6d2de3"
        },
        "kind": "documentation",
        "reference": {
          "path": "docs/XERJ_VS_LUCENE.md",
          "content_hash": "sha256:118ab10d635e0eae325c47f0ec357317b16357dd3a1c41b77fba45fb8b92dbcc",
          "start_line": 17,
          "end_line": 31,
          "excerpt": "source wins if a nearby overview page says something different.\n\nThe default XERJ embedding fallback is lexical feature-hashing, not neural\nsemantic understanding ([`Embedder`](https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj/blob/24711999dd866ceec2a6e7c91d934c2c27d7066c/engine/crates/xerj-ai/src/embedder.rs#L7-L23)).\nThe built-in neural BERT backend is opt-in via `--embed-mode neural` and\ndownloads its model on first use ([model loader](https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj/blob/24711999dd866ceec2a6e7c91d934c2c27d7066c/engine/crates/xerj-ai/src/neural.rs#L225-L275)).\n\n| Axis | Lucene 10.3.1 | XERJ at `24711999` |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Segment and merge model | `IndexWriter`, immutable per-segment lifecycle, merge policy and scheduler | WAL, sharded buffers, immutable `.seg` containers and sidecars |\n| 2. Postings layout | BlockTree terms, packed blocks, two-level impact skips | FST/metadata terms, 128-doc PFOR blocks, no persisted skip table |\n| 3. Values and ranges | DocValues for columns; BKD points for numeric and geo ranges | Numeric/keyword `.dv` columns with a sorted range index |\n| 4. Analysis chain | Broad analysis modules and composable `CustomAnalyzer` | Curated registry and shape-specific query projection |\n| 5. Update and delete semantics | Delete/add documents plus restricted DocValues updates | Source overlay, logical replacement, versions and tombstones |\n| 6. Vector index placement | Per-segment HNSW, filter-aware search and quantized codecs | Index-level HNSW for eligible plain queries; exact fallback elsewhere |"
        },
        "origin": "UNINTERPRETED_EXCERPT",
        "matched_question_terms": [
          "xerj"
        ],
