      {
        "id": "card_5a9afbe97291845016ddeec731ed8f009e83aa96cc76d292ea243f394465bcf0",
        "source": {
          "repository": "xerj-org/xerj",
          "commit": "1557de2f5be981d9db441969201c92a8af6d2de3"
        },
        "kind": "documentation",
        "reference": {
          "path": "demo/playbooks/MIXED_READ_UNDER_WRITE_FINDING_2026-07-08.md",
          "content_hash": "sha256:3cec79d6e4f320fda6d756408ff5f1626c0271695e7df637290d27b4321422e0",
          "start_line": 73,
          "end_line": 88,
          "excerpt": "- The contention is on **`FtsMemtable` per-shard `parking_lot::RwLock`.** Stacks\n  show readers parked in `RwLock::read`→`lock_shared_slow` and a writer parked\n  in `RwLock::write`→`wait_for_readers` — the classic parking_lot\n  writer-preference cascade (new readers queue behind a waiting writer). Also\n  ~294 `xerj-rt` runtime threads exist (worker+blocking pool), almost all\n  parked.\n- The slow range-agg READ itself has NO frames on any stack → it is\n  **async-suspended at an `.await`**, waiting, not running.\n\n**CRITICAL REPRO CORRECTION (honesty — my numbers were unrepresentative):**\n`scratchpad/load_driver.py` wrote with **explicit `_id`s** →\n`process_bulk_with_opts`→`index_document`→`ShardedFtsMemtable::remove`\n(memtable.rs:619) takes a shard **write lock PER DOCUMENT** (remove-before-\ninsert). The real benchmark (`bench-matrix.mjs:424,470`) writes **auto-id\n`{\"index\":{}}`** → the turbo/chunked path (one write lock per ~512-doc chunk).\nSo my ~20 s stalls are **amplified ~100×** by an unrepresentative write path;"
        },
        "origin": "UNINTERPRETED_EXCERPT",
