        "kind": "example",
        "reference": {
          "path": "docs/examples/anomaly-detection/anomaly_detection.py",
          "content_hash": "sha256:124b5641a6c5aa4b3280115b2ff01b6816baac77828c6c8a6ba9341a7728e959",
          "start_line": 1,
          "end_line": 16,
          "excerpt": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nAnomaly detection on a metric series with XERJ.\n\nScenario: we collect per-host CPU readings into `cpu_metrics`. For fifteen\nminutes CPU sits around ~20%. At minute 12 a runaway process pins the box and\nthe per-minute mean jumps to ~96%, then recovers. We want XERJ to flag that one\nminute as anomalous - automatically, without us hand-picking a threshold on the\nraw value.\n\nXERJ's on-demand anomaly detector does exactly this: it buckets the source\nindex by time, computes the metric per bucket (here mean(cpu)), builds a moving\nbaseline from prior *normal* buckets, and scores each bucket by how many\nstandard deviations it sits from that baseline.\n\nRun:  python3 anomaly_detection.py                       # assumes XERJ on :9200"
        },
        "origin": "UNINTERPRETED_EXCERPT",
        "matched_question_terms": [
          "xerj"
        ],
        "distinct_excerpt_words": 73,
        "familiar_substring_matches": [],
        "selection_reasons": [
          "LITERAL_QUESTION_TERM_MATCH"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "card_374bba7ecb3ab8b064767b1242dce48b542a021b690697b8dc48feb5df8a6989",
        "source": {
          "repository": "xerj-org/xerj",
          "commit": "1557de2f5be981d9db441969201c92a8af6d2de3"
        },
        "kind": "file",
        "reference": {
          "path": "demo/agent-gate/make_corpus_prose.py",
          "content_hash": "sha256:c894e2d48dd2111ca751d37a4c1b9cb47d283f9295113f56e5486b993f197b0f",
          "start_line": 1,
          "end_line": 16,
          "excerpt": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Deterministic PROSE/CODE-heavy corpus for the Agent Gate — the regime where\nXERJ is expected to WIN on tokens.\n\nThe mixed corpus (make_corpus.py) is 99.99% structured records, where grep on a\none-integer question is unbeatable. This corpus is the opposite: many small\ndocuments of natural-language and source text, no large record streams. It is\nthe shape of a real code/knowledge repository, and it is where ranked retrieval\nbeats unranked grep on tokens — grep must return every candidate line, ranked\nsearch returns the one passage.\n\nSeeded, so runs are byte-identical and comparable across versions.\nUsage: make_corpus_prose.py \u003cdir\u003e\n\"\"\"\nimport os\nimport random"
        },
        "origin": "UNINTERPRETED_EXCERPT",
        "matched_question_terms": [
          "xerj"
        ],
        "distinct_excerpt_words": 69,
        "familiar_substring_matches": [],
        "selection_reasons": [
          "LITERAL_QUESTION_TERM_MATCH"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "card_48acf6317b30ba0a54536c6c08202d6ae91c68c01032c38abcd95b33847bd2ff",
        "source": {
          "repository": "xerj-org/xerj",
          "commit": "1557de2f5be981d9db441969201c92a8af6d2de3"
        },
        "kind": "file",
        "reference": {
          "path": "demo/data/extras/generate_demo_corpus.py",
          "content_hash": "sha256:772f84718a1c2984b541666413443ab659e70744efd5dc72873481a5752d8517",
          "start_line": 1,
          "end_line": 16,
          "excerpt": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Generate realistic-shaped demo corpora for the Xerj Console dashboards.\n\nWrites one NDJSON file per intended index under demo/data/extras/:\n\n  chat-events.ndjson   — LLM query telemetry (drives ai-overview / rag-quality)\n  vector-ops.ndjson    — vector index events (drives vector-index)\n  agent-memory.ndjson  — agent memory operations (drives agent-memory)\n  anomalies.ndjson     — anomaly detector findings (drives anomaly-detect)\n  ingest-events.ndjson — ingest pipeline events (drives ingest-pipeline)\n\nTimestamps span the last 24h so the dashboards' default 24H range\ncaptures everything. Distributions are seeded for reproducibility.\n\"\"\"\nimport json, random, time, math, sys, os\nrandom.seed(42)"
        },
        "origin": "UNINTERPRETED_EXCERPT",
        "matched_question_terms": [
          "xerj"
        ],
        "distinct_excerpt_words": 64,
        "familiar_substring_matches": [],
        "selection_reasons": [
          "LITERAL_QUESTION_TERM_MATCH"
        ]
      },
